  "result": "The retry configuration for webhook deliveries is split across two files:\n\n- **`src/server/jobs/webhook-delivery-job.ts`** defines webhook-specific retry limits:\n  - `MAX_ATTEMPTS = 6` (line 22) - how many times a webhook delivery is attempted\n  - `backoffMs()` function (lines 90-93) - exponential backoff capped at 5 minutes\n\n- **`src/server/jobs/queue.ts`** defines the general job queue retry mechanism:\n  - `MAX_ATTEMPTS = 5` (line 26) - general job retry limit\n  - `backoffMs()` function (lines 107-109) - exponential backoff capped at 1 minute\n\nWhen a customer's server is down, webhook delivery jobs are retried through both systems: the webhook-delivery-job retries individual deliveries up to 6 times with exponential backoff, and if the entire job fails, the queue system retries the job itself up to 5 times.\n\nANSWER: src/server/jobs/queue.ts, src/server/jobs/webhook-delivery-job.ts",
